{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question","id":1204711,"title":"DragonBlooded Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-08T15:53:34-07:00","id":1204711,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> DragonBlooded Question","content":"So reading over the new stuff. I see there are parts about the Dragonblooded using Numina and another being part demon. So my question is what combinations of Dragonblooded are there because I thought only the Dragonblooded exaltation can take hold on someone who is only normal mortal. Not someone who is crafted raced, beastman, or blooded (god, demon, ghost or fae)? If so where can I find this information in previous editions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:00:17-07:00","id":1204715,"title":"","content":"All of the Exaltations can affect god-blooded, demon-blooded, ghost-blooded, fae-blooded and elemental-blooded. It's just not common (because, I guess, those are not common).<br /> It was in 2nd edition... Scroll of Heroes, I think? The rules were terrible though. But they did explicitly let you play a Demon-Blooded Solar or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:22:00-07:00","id":1204722,"title":"","content":"Dragon-Blooded Lintha were also mentioned in Compass: West, and Dragon-Blooded Hawkmen (at least as a theoretical possibility) in Compass: East.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:27:04-07:00","id":1204725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question#post1204711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reading over the new stuff. I see there are parts about the Dragonblooded using Numina and another being part demon. So my question is what combinations of Dragonblooded are there because I thought only the Dragonblooded exaltation can take hold on someone who is only normal mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The additional powers of Forest Witches (the numina) are actually something that comes later, from association with the Sea of Mind, rather than something inborn.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut for the rest, yeah, the image of the Dragon Blooded with a storm demon ancestor has been enduring enough that there have been varying degrees of wanting to build around accommodating it, which I think may be strongest in this Edition.<br /> <br /> \u200bReally, between those two and some weird possibilities given for outcastes in the new book, I speculate that one implication they're running with is that the lower overall power of Terrestrials makes them more amenable to having some additional kinds of power overlaying them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not someone who is crafted raced</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI know you're referring to the slave races of the First Age, but a funny thing is that with the more explicit reference to the Dragon's blood as being something metaphysical, it's now something that can be passed on even to a child manufactured by some form of sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:31:21-07:00","id":1204727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question#post1204711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reading over the new stuff. I see there are parts about the Dragonblooded using Numina and another being part demon. So my question is what combinations of Dragonblooded are there because I thought only the Dragonblooded exaltation can take hold on someone who is only normal mortal. Not someone who is crafted raced, beastman, or blooded (god, demon, ghost or fae)? If so where can I find this information in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exaltation in general can attach to anyone. The reaosn that Dragon-Blooded <i>normally</i> aren't also something like a sort of god-blood (which si the catch-all for the children of superantural beings) is more that such beings in themselves are pretty rare. When there might be a million of them, only twenty-five thousand Terrestrial Exalted, and hundreds of milliions of people in the world, the chances of anyone being one of both are pretty slim.<br /> <br /> Crafted races (if they even exist in 3e) and beastmen are typically just humans, just very strange ones. Nothing about Exaltation, Dragon-Blooded or otherwise, interferes iwht that really.<br /> <br /> Previous editions talked about this some. Usually it was through a bit of an xp-penalty system for god-blooded mixed with Exalted, but due to the structure of how god-blooded working might not be the same in 3e, it's probably manifest more often as weird unique Merits and such anyhow for an Exalt. There's nothing really mechancial preventing it.<br /> <br /> Numina, it should noted are actually something else here. They're indivdiuals who have made a deal or joined the Mist that the Forest Witches deal with and are kind of an exotic transformation some Dragon-Blooded have gone thorugh to become a different sort of being. Whether they can even be not Dragon-Blooded isn't clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:32:39-07:00","id":1204728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question#post1204711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reading over the new stuff. I see there are parts about the Dragonblooded using Numina and another being part demon. So my question is what combinations of Dragonblooded are there because I thought only the Dragonblooded exaltation can take hold on someone who is only normal mortal. Not someone who is crafted raced, beastman, or blooded (god, demon, ghost or fae)? If so where can I find this information in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The 1st edition player's guide let Exalted PCs of any type start with the Inheritance Background to reflect being God-Blooded. It deducted your starting charms, and I think may have put a surcharge on Essence xp, but you had bonus starting points for mutations, relelvant charms, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T16:48:43-07:00","id":1204742,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that, mostly what you would get from being God-Blooded or whatever, in pretty much any edition, is access to Supernatural Merits and maybe access to a couple of custom charms. In this edition, between Sorcery and Artifact Evocations, you can just buy Supernatural Merits and get access to nearly any kind of custom charm you want via evocations. So, there's little reason to deny someone the opportunity to be a Beastperson Solar or a Demon Blooded Dragon Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T19:27:48-07:00","id":1205057,"title":"","content":"Speaking of demons and crafted, it's mentioned that Neomah are used in secret by infertile couples to produce heirs that can attain Terrestrial Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T21:48:31-07:00","id":1205092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question#post1204711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So reading over the new stuff. I see there are parts about the Dragonblooded using Numina and another being part demon. So my question is what combinations of Dragonblooded are there because I thought only the Dragonblooded exaltation can take hold on someone who is only normal mortal. Not someone who is crafted raced, beastman, or blooded (god, demon, ghost or fae)? If so where can I find this information in previous editions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall more of a rolepaying element than anything, overall as Ledaal Kebok Coren has been a canon element since at least 1e' Dragon-Bblooded.<br /> Where one might get some actual crunch was 1e's PG and 2e's Scroll of Heroes with their respective god-blooded rules, though mechanic or actual practical use might be up to debate, YMMV.<br /> <br /> One way i see that one might use to adapt the concept of god-bloods - in particular the idea of touching upon the powers of one's spirit parent (or even distant ancestor in more particular cases) - could be to treat this &quot;Inheritance&quot; as a supernatural merit one unlocks Evocations related to that spirit's legend/legacy from, much like an Artifact. Who knows, the Inheritance could manifest itself as a literal Artifact reflecting that being's own panoply. Would be pretty appropriate/consistent in fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question?p=1205057#post1205057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of demons and crafted, it's mentioned that Neomah are used in secret by infertile couples to produce heirs that can attain Terrestrial Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that from 2e, but ain't sure it is still kosher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-10-2018, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T22:18:47-07:00","id":1205096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question?p=1205092#post1205092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that from 2e, but ain't sure it is still kosher.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 3e stuff that has been released mentions demons as one way, amongst many, for an otherwise infertile couple to conceive children that have the chance of bearing the spark of DB Exaltation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T22:25:08-07:00","id":1205098,"title":"","content":"Mind the protocols do seem to just be methods of enabling couples incapable of conception through normal biological means to still produce their own offspring, but not a case of someone using sorcery/demons/what have you to just create offspring and give them the ability to exalt DB without the prereq of at least a parent capable of passing down the potential.<br /> <br /> Just saying it, so its on the record in case someone got the wrong idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T22:29:12-07:00","id":1205099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question?p=1205096#post1205096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 3e stuff that has been released mentions demons as one way, amongst many, for an otherwise infertile couple to conceive children that have the chance of bearing the spark of DB Exaltation.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, but without actual mechanics that offer actual bonuses to exaltation chances of the child this time around, i guess, as getting around infertility as a complication is bonus aplenty might be said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T00:10:46-07:00","id":1205115,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about &quot;bonuses to Exaltation chances?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T01:54:34-07:00","id":1205123,"title":"","content":"Heirs created via neomah have the exact same chance to exalt as they would if they were born naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:42:39-07:00","id":1205260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question?p=1205115#post1205115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said anything about &quot;bonuses to Exaltation chances?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>True, i'm probably the one most to blame for that, but it's the kind of... ripe 2e corpse i really wanted to put to rest and keep buried. My overzealous bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 04-10-2018, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:03:38-07:00","id":1205296,"title":"","content":"If I understood the Ask the Developers Thread correctly it would be possible for a Solar or Lunar of Dragon Blood parents to have a child that was Dragon Blooded. Which could make for a very interesting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T11:20:24-07:00","id":1205304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1204711-dragonblooded-question?p=1205296#post1205296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I understood the Ask the Developers Thread correctly it would be possible for a Solar or Lunar of Dragon Blood parents to have a child that was Dragon Blooded. Which could make for a very interesting character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sort of a Dragon-Blooded Half-Caste (Solar/Lunar) sort of thing? An interesting idea to be sure, but we will have to wait to see if Half Castes are still a thing in this Ex3... and even if they are, becoming a Dragon-Blood may burn out such potential as a Half-Caste as they are becoming a full Exalt (a little lesser than their Solar/Lunar parent, but still an Exalt). Where as other God-Blood heritages are from other supernatural beings that are not Exalted (and thus at least theoretically) can coexist with the Exaltation... at least to a small degree (again, to what extent remains to be seen).<br /> <br /> Regardless... it will likely be some time before we see anything along these lines. It may be possible that the developers may include God-Blooded creation with the Exigent book... as the God-Blooded may need custom charms similar to those these unique Exalts may receive... but I would say that is a long shot at best (and likely to be a very unlikely development).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T03:07:43-07:00","id":1205518,"title":"","content":"I think a dragon blooded child of a solar or lunar would, at best, be allowed to get some solar or lunar themed merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive",